    "result_text": "That \"ERROR\" is just the word appearing inside a Spring Security WARN message \u2014 not an actual error. The build is green.\n\nThe change is complete. Here's a summary of what I implemented:\n\n## Summary\n\nAdded a structured address form to the owner-create flow while keeping the flat `address` input backward-compatible.\n\n**API contract** (`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`)\n- Added optional `addressLine1` and `addressLine2` to the `OwnerFields` schema (which flows into both the request DTO and the response `Owner` DTO via the generator).\n- Removed `address` from the `required` list so structured-only payloads pass bean validation; documented `address` as the composed, normalized read value.\n\n**Domain model** (`Owner.java`)\n- Added `addressLine1` / `addressLine2` fields (`address_line1`, `address_line2` columns) with getters/setters. MapStruct maps them by name in both directions with no mapper changes.\n\n**Database schema** (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres `schema.sql`)\n- Added nullable `address_line1` / `address_line2` columns to the `owners` table.\n\n**Controller** (`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`)\n- Replaced the single flat-address normalization with a new `applyAddress` helper that:\n  - Normalizes whichever address fields are supplied (reusing the existing `normalizeAddress` rules \u2014 trim, collapse whitespace, upper-case, expand `ST\u2192STREET` etc.).\n  - Prefers the structured form: when `addressLine1` is non-blank, the composed `address` is the normalized `addressLine1`, with a single space + normalized `addressLine2` appended when line 2 is present; otherwise it falls back to the normalized flat `address`.\n  - Writes the normalized structured fields and the composed `address` back onto the DTO, so everything downstream (household hash, postcode validation, locality, storage, response) reads the resolved address. When neither form is supplied the composed value is blank, so the existing required-field check rejects it.\n\nBoth acceptance tests (`coreNormalizesAndComposesStructuredAddress`, `functionalityStillAcceptsFlatAddress`) pass, and the full suite is green (`Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`).",
